      "why_additions_occur_unchecked": "Although every AllowedSPI-legacy.toml file starts with `# NEVER add to this list, only remove!`, neither `webkitapipy/allow.py` nor `webkitpy/style/checkers/spi_allowlist.py` enforces a non-growth check on `AllowedSPI-legacy.toml` (`spi_allowlist.py` only checks whether bug URLs contain 'OOPS'). Furthermore, `allow.py` requires `cleanup` or `request` radar URLs for entries in `AllowedSPI.toml` (`[[temporary-usage]]`, `[[not-web-essential]]`, `[[equivalent-api]]`), whereas `[[legacy]]` blocks in `AllowedSPI-legacy.toml` require no bug URLs—creating a path of least resistance for unreviewed or newly-surfaced SPIs."
