      "author": "Elliott Williams",
      "subject": "[SPI Checking] Fix cookie partitioning SPI in WebKit's allowlist https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=298415 rdar://159885742",
      "description": "Reviewed by Brianna Fan.\n\nSome of the implementation of partitioning is controlled by the\nENABLE_OPT_IN_PARTITIONED_COOKIES flag, which is not enabled in all\ninternal builds performing SPI checking. This caused us to miss these\nneeded allowlist entries during bringup of audit-spi.\n\nFix by adding what's needed, with the appropriate `requires` conditions.\n\n* Source/WebKit/Configurations/AllowedSPI.toml: Of note,\n  -cookieTransformCallback: is only accessed from an assertion, so it's\n  not active SPI use in release builds and must be guarded by\n  ASSERT_ENABLED.\n\nCanonical link: https://commits.webkit.org/299592@main",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/098c5e4bc8d260160d0b3fa38761e0d710895937",
      "bugs": [
        "https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=298415",
        "rdar://159885742"
      ],
      "primary_category": "build-or-conditional-fix",
      "feature_area": "Privacy, ITP & Content Filtering",
      "why_changed": "Fixed build conditions for partitioned cookies SPI by adding ENABLE_OPT_IN_PARTITIONED_COOKIES and ASSERT_ENABLED requirements for NSURLSessionTask selectors.",
      "legacy_addition_category": null,
      "legacy_addition_reason": null,
      "touched_toml_files": [
        "Source/WebKit/Configurations/AllowedSPI.toml"
      ],
      "other_touched_files_count": 0,
