      "author": "Youenn Fablet",
      "subject": "[iOS 26] Camera capture orientation is not correct on SafariViewService rdar://160105158 https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=300428",
      "description": "Reviewed by Wenson Hsieh.\n\nOn iOS 26, UIApplication.sharedApplication.statusBarOrientation seems to always return the portrait orientation on SVC.\nwindowScene.effectiveGeometry.interfaceOrientation on the other end provides the correct value.\nWe switch the order to use windowScene.effectiveGeometry.interfaceOrientation if there is a scene and UIApplication.sharedApplication.statusBarOrientation otherwise.\nWe also remove one UIKit SPI as part of this change.\n\nManually tested on Mobile Safari, SVC and WKWebView.\n\nCanonical link: https://commits.webkit.org/301262@main",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/3c51043d4a3956629cd5dddfc3a52847564786ac",
      "bugs": [
        "https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=300428",
        "rdar://160105158"
      ],
      "primary_category": "cleanup-remove-spi",
      "feature_area": "Media, Audio & Video",
      "why_changed": "Switched camera capture orientation checking to use public scene lifecycle APIs, eliminating UIApplication _appAdoptsUISceneLifecycle SPI selector.",
      "legacy_addition_category": null,
      "legacy_addition_reason": null,
